{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"e01687d8-39e4-4f92-932f-19adbdb5612b","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The causes of the failure and the fixes applied have been analyzed and documented in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-O0vi2M/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary of Causes\n\nInspection of `Library/Logs/nightly-review.err` and `launchctl-print.txt` revealed two stacked issues:\n\n1. **Missing `USER` environment variable in launchd (`Not logged in · Please run /login`)**:\n   Under launchd, `claude` CLI cannot find user credentials/keychain data without the `USER` environment variable set. The plist only defined `PATH` in `EnvironmentVariables`, causing `claude` to fail immediately.\n2. **Assigning to read-only built-in variable `status` in zsh (`read-only variable: status`)**:\n   In [nightly-review.zsh](file:///tmp/h-O0vi2M/bin/nightly-review.zsh#L19), the script executed `status=$?`. In `zsh`, `status` is a built-in read-only variable (an alias for `$?`). Assigning to it caused a fatal error, terminating the script immediately before reaching the failure notification line (`\"$NOTIFY\" \"nightly review FAILED...\"`).\n\n### Fixes Applied\n\n- [Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist](file:///tmp/h-O0vi2M/Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist): Added `USER` (`vk`) to `EnvironmentVariables`.\n- [bin/nightly-review.zsh](file:///tmp/h-O0vi2M/bin/nightly-review.zsh): Changed `status=$?` to `rc=$?` (and updated references to `$rc`). Also redirected stdin from `/dev/null` (`\u003c /dev/null`) to ensure unattended runs do not block waiting on stdin.\n","duration_seconds":80.240819,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":129611,"output_tokens":2686,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":210662,"total_tokens":132297}}}
